==English==

===Etymology===
{{etyl|enm|en}}, from {{etyl|fro|en}} {{m|fro|residu}}, from {{etyl|la|en}} {{m|la|residuum}}, neuter of {{m|la|residuus||remaining}}, from {{m|la|resideō||I remain behind}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|GenAm}} {{IPA|/ˈɹɛzɪduː/|lang=en}}
* {{a|RP}} {{IPA|/ˈɹɛzɪdjuː/|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# Whatever [[remain]]s after something else has been [[removed]].
# {{label|en|chemistry}} The [[substance]] that remains after [[evaporation]], [[distillation]], [[filtration]] or any similar process.
# {{label|en|biochemistry}} An [[amino acid]] forming part of a [[polypeptide]] chain.
# {{label|en|legal}} Whatever [[property]] or [[effect]]s are left in an [[estate]] after payment of all debts, other charges and deduction of what is specifically [[bequeathed]] by the [[testator]].
# {{label|en|mathematics}} A form of [[complex number]], [[proportional]] to the [[contour integral]] of a [[meromorphic]] [[function]] along a [[path]] enclosing one of its [[singularity|singularities]].

